1
00:00:07,560 --> 00:00:09,260
What do you want to do?

2
00:00:09,380 --> 00:00:11,130
Who are you?

3
00:00:11,130 --> 00:00:13,350
Me? I'm the owner of this house.

4
00:00:14,490 --> 00:00:16,940
That's the destiny.

5
00:00:17,790 --> 00:00:20,210
I never sold this place.

6
00:00:20,210 --> 00:00:22,100
Get out.

7
00:00:22,100 --> 00:00:24,720
I don't want to stay here.

8
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:28,750
I want you out by the end of this week.

9
00:00:28,750 --> 00:00:31,140
If not, you'll be gone with this building.

10
00:00:31,140 --> 00:00:33,880
No way, this is my house.

11
00:00:33,880 --> 00:00:35,700
You have no right to do that.

12
00:00:35,700 --> 00:00:38,460
Why do you keep torturing me and following me around?

13
00:00:38,460 --> 00:00:40,960
Who are you? Why are you doing this to me?

14
00:00:40,960 --> 00:00:44,130
What a bad person you are to treat me like this.

15
00:00:44,130 --> 00:00:48,890
How can you do this to me?

16
00:00:50,610 --> 00:00:54,470
Do you think what you did was okay?

17
00:00:54,470 --> 00:00:57,730
How did it feel when you walked away from a dying person?

18
00:00:57,730 --> 00:00:59,650
What I've done

19
00:00:59,650 --> 00:01:01,040
is nothing.

20
00:01:01,040 --> 00:01:04,190
Compared to what you took away from me.

21
00:01:06,750 --> 00:01:09,430
Don't show up in front of me

22
00:01:09,890 --> 00:01:13,430
by the end of this week.

23
00:02:02,280 --> 00:02:03,960
Are you done crying?

24
00:02:07,460 --> 00:02:11,330
You think I'm pathetic, don't you?

25
00:02:14,700 --> 00:02:16,450
A little bit.

26
00:02:18,390 --> 00:02:21,730
It would be better if he listened to your song till the end.

27
00:02:24,270 --> 00:02:26,480
This is what I think.

28
00:02:27,440 --> 00:02:32,560
Don't cry for someone who won't cry for you.

29
00:02:36,060 --> 00:02:37,750
Wipe away your tears.

30
00:02:37,750 --> 00:02:44,480
Why don't you cry for someone who'll cry for you?

31
00:03:09,300 --> 00:03:13,180
What should I do with the house?

32
00:03:13,450 --> 00:03:16,750
Just leave it.

33
00:03:19,860 --> 00:03:23,430
Stop stalking Kang Yoo Jung now.

34
00:03:24,050 --> 00:03:25,300
Yes, sir!

35
00:03:29,170 --> 00:03:30,580
So annoyed.

36
00:03:41,730 --> 00:03:43,580
Was that you?

37
00:03:43,880 --> 00:03:48,110
You can't just hit people and run away.

38
00:03:50,490 --> 00:03:52,460
Because of you.

39
00:03:52,510 --> 00:03:55,010
How dare you hurt what's mine?

40
00:03:55,140 --> 00:03:58,790
Don't look at me with innocent eyes.

41
00:03:58,790 --> 00:04:00,590
Why are you doing this to me?

42
00:04:00,590 --> 00:04:05,150
Why do you have to torture me like this?

43
00:04:05,150 --> 00:04:08,040
Just stay in jail.

44
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:11,980
When you get out, I'll make your life miserable.

45
00:04:17,040 --> 00:04:20,050
Yoo Jung!

46
00:04:20,050 --> 00:04:21,070
Do Hoon!

47
00:04:21,070 --> 00:04:23,290
What's going on?

48
00:04:23,290 --> 00:04:25,460
Nothing! It's okay.

49
00:04:25,460 --> 00:04:28,840
Let me see. Are you hurt?

50
00:04:28,840 --> 00:04:31,520
We have to move out.

51
00:04:31,520 --> 00:04:33,940
The landlord came.

52
00:04:33,940 --> 00:04:36,150
He wants us out by the end of the week.

53
00:04:36,150 --> 00:04:39,720
This is so sudden. Let me talk to him.

54
00:04:39,720 --> 00:04:41,760
Don't.

55
00:04:41,820 --> 00:04:43,460
I'll take care of it. Don't worry.

56
00:04:43,460 --> 00:04:44,100
But...

57
00:04:44,100 --> 00:04:46,260
He won't listen to you.

58
00:04:46,260 --> 00:04:52,070
I'll talk to him. Let me deal with him.

59
00:04:59,190 --> 00:05:01,920
I do owe him money.

60
00:05:27,390 --> 00:05:29,350
What are you doing here?

61
00:05:31,110 --> 00:05:35,790
I don't know what I'm doing here.

62
00:05:38,280 --> 00:05:40,360
Aren't you going home?

63
00:05:41,890 --> 00:05:45,670
Home? I have nothing to do there.

64
00:05:47,000 --> 00:05:49,220
Did something happen?

65
00:05:51,380 --> 00:05:53,550
Something?

66
00:05:57,360 --> 00:06:00,640
Is it about you singing in public?

67
00:06:01,510 --> 00:06:04,930
You've had stage fright since you were little.

68
00:06:04,940 --> 00:06:08,270
Who did you want to impress?

69
00:06:08,270 --> 00:06:12,390
You don't normally sing on stage for no reason.

70
00:06:16,630 --> 00:06:22,020
Jo Min Hyuk! I didn't sing for anyone else.

71
00:06:24,350 --> 00:06:27,160
I did it for you.

72
00:06:33,520 --> 00:06:36,160
Was that your present for me?

73
00:06:36,160 --> 00:06:40,750
You already have everything,

74
00:06:41,750 --> 00:06:43,800
I can do nothing but sing for you.

75
00:06:43,800 --> 00:06:48,300
Why didn't you tell me earlier? I happened to...

76
00:06:48,300 --> 00:06:51,880
I'm off. I'm getting tired.

77
00:06:54,220 --> 00:06:55,850
Se Yeon!

78
00:06:57,460 --> 00:07:00,320
Can't you sing now?

79
00:07:00,320 --> 00:07:03,210
You want me to listen, right?

80
00:07:07,930 --> 00:07:10,410
Min Hyuk.

81
00:07:13,520 --> 00:07:16,720
Do you think you can cry for me?

82
00:07:19,330 --> 00:07:23,560
Can you cry for me?

83
00:07:32,560 --> 00:07:37,610
What is this? It's so unlike you.

84
00:07:39,810 --> 00:07:41,770
I'm done.

85
00:07:41,770 --> 00:07:42,570
What?

86
00:07:42,570 --> 00:07:47,960
This marriage.

87
00:08:35,190 --> 00:08:38,450
How did it feel when you walked away from a dying person?

88
00:08:38,450 --> 00:08:40,360
This building?

89
00:08:40,360 --> 00:08:41,820
This is nothing.

90
00:08:41,820 --> 00:08:44,910
Compared to what you took away from me.

91
00:08:52,090 --> 00:08:56,770
Dad, we have to go.

92
00:09:01,250 --> 00:09:03,380
Let's go traveling.

93
00:09:03,380 --> 00:09:07,790
Let's go to see the sea and mountains.

94
00:09:09,640 --> 00:09:10,990
Sea.

95
00:09:11,020 --> 00:09:14,560
Let's go on a trip.

96
00:09:14,560 --> 00:09:16,610
Good. Sea.

97
00:09:17,050 --> 00:09:18,550
Let's go.

98
00:09:22,860 --> 00:09:26,770
Take this off. It's itchy.

99
00:09:26,870 --> 00:09:29,680
No. You have to wear it all the time.

100
00:09:29,680 --> 00:09:36,630
Take it off. Please take it off.

101
00:09:41,730 --> 00:09:43,640
Dad! Dad!

102
00:09:44,920 --> 00:09:47,480
Dad! Dad!

103
00:09:47,480 --> 00:09:50,280
Dad! Dad!

104
00:09:54,540 --> 00:10:00,030
Forty-five, forty-six, forty-seven.

105
00:10:00,310 --> 00:10:03,680
When I was your age, I had no fat around my belly.

106
00:10:03,680 --> 00:10:05,470
I was so fit.

107
00:10:05,470 --> 00:10:06,690
Mom!

108
00:10:06,690 --> 00:10:08,490
Five more!

109
00:10:12,160 --> 00:10:13,460
You're not born with a perfect body.

110
00:10:13,460 --> 00:10:16,750
It depends on how much effort you put into it.

111
00:10:16,750 --> 00:10:18,240
If I had your genes,

112
00:10:18,240 --> 00:10:20,110
I wouldn't have to do this.

113
00:10:20,110 --> 00:10:22,670
Why do I have daddy's genes?

114
00:10:23,260 --> 00:10:25,110
Yes.

115
00:10:27,680 --> 00:10:30,750
I wish you had my genes, too.

116
00:10:31,950 --> 00:10:35,960
I don't look like you at all.

117
00:10:35,960 --> 00:10:38,230
So do my eating habits and fit.

118
00:10:38,230 --> 00:10:39,700
You know what my friends say?

119
00:10:39,700 --> 00:10:42,890
You and I don't look alike at all.

120
00:10:42,970 --> 00:10:46,270
Mom, do you...

121
00:10:46,360 --> 00:10:47,460
What?

122
00:10:47,460 --> 00:10:50,840
Tell me the truth. I'm not a kid anymore.

123
00:10:50,840 --> 00:10:51,620
What?

124
00:10:51,620 --> 00:10:56,020
Did you get plastic surgery?

125
00:10:59,330 --> 00:11:03,370
Absolutely not!

126
00:11:03,370 --> 00:11:04,490
I was born pretty.

127
00:11:04,490 --> 00:11:05,810
Tell me! Where?

128
00:11:05,810 --> 00:11:06,940
Stop!

129
00:11:06,940 --> 00:11:08,180
Tell me! Come on!

130
00:11:08,180 --> 00:11:09,910
Okay! Okay! My eyes!

131
00:11:09,910 --> 00:11:11,610
Where else?

132
00:11:23,450 --> 00:11:24,440
Se Yeon, the other day...

133
00:11:24,460 --> 00:11:26,550
Come on in.

134
00:11:33,180 --> 00:11:37,450
What? Don't you want to cancel the wedding?

135
00:11:37,460 --> 00:11:42,050
This is a business.

136
00:11:42,060 --> 00:11:49,270
This is a good opportunity to cooperate, and this is the prenup. I already signed it.

137
00:11:52,220 --> 00:11:56,790
This is a Lucida Diamond cut in 1999.

138
00:11:59,030 --> 00:12:01,360
It belongs to princeess series.

139
00:12:01,380 --> 00:12:05,200
I don't care about that. What's the most expensive ring?

140
00:12:07,520 --> 00:12:08,650
What about that one?

141
00:12:08,660 --> 00:12:10,080
That one?

142
00:12:10,090 --> 00:12:12,170
What? It's really big.

143
00:12:12,180 --> 00:12:16,810
Give me the biggest or the most expensive ring in the world,

144
00:12:16,830 --> 00:12:22,590
If not, get me the one you'd want me to have.

145
00:12:26,640 --> 00:12:30,560
You don't want to give me anything?

146
00:12:30,580 --> 00:12:34,510
- All the rings are the same. - I'll have that one.

147
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:40,440
The more I get the better.

148
00:12:40,450 --> 00:12:42,030
Are you going to take penalty if I breach the prenup?

149
00:12:42,030 --> 00:12:44,210
Of course.

150
00:12:46,430 --> 00:12:49,260
It's all written here. Read it carefully.

151
00:12:49,270 --> 00:12:54,340
Whoever violates this contract first will pay.

152
00:12:58,530 --> 00:13:01,920
If I give you the ring, what will you give me?

153
00:13:01,940 --> 00:13:06,030
I can increase your value by marrying you.

154
00:13:06,040 --> 00:13:07,640
Hey, Se Yeon!

155
00:13:07,660 --> 00:13:11,710
Thank you for the ring.

156
00:13:29,120 --> 00:13:32,740
She sure is Shin's daughter.

157
00:13:32,750 --> 00:13:35,350
They only care about themselves.

158
00:13:35,360 --> 00:13:36,830
You know Se Yeon is not like that.

159
00:13:36,830 --> 00:13:38,010
Grow up.

160
00:13:38,020 --> 00:13:40,000
We've been friends since elementary school.

161
00:13:40,010 --> 00:13:45,020
Friends? Stop being silly.

162
00:13:45,030 --> 00:13:50,000
You know who your real friends are when you're in need.

163
00:13:51,990 --> 00:13:56,180
Go over it, make some necessary changes, and send it back.

164
00:13:56,190 --> 00:13:58,590
Yes, sir!

165
00:14:06,370 --> 00:14:09,680
Has Kang Yoo Jung moved out?

166
00:14:10,980 --> 00:14:12,630
I told her to move out by the end of this week.

167
00:14:12,630 --> 00:14:17,490
You told me not to follow her around, so...

168
00:14:19,450 --> 00:14:23,880
But you stil have to know where she is.

169
00:14:24,350 --> 00:14:26,370
I'm sorry.

170
00:14:26,390 --> 00:14:29,160
I've lost my appetite.

171
00:14:33,500 --> 00:14:36,970
You shouldn't have come here.

172
00:14:36,990 --> 00:14:38,740
I know Do Hoon sent you here,

173
00:14:38,750 --> 00:14:41,340
but you shouldn't have come here with your father.

174
00:14:41,360 --> 00:14:42,070
Mother!

175
00:14:42,070 --> 00:14:44,670
Stop! People might misunderstand that.

176
00:14:44,690 --> 00:14:48,430
I'm not your mother. We're not family.

177
00:14:49,270 --> 00:14:51,820
I'm sorry.Mo...

178
00:14:52,410 --> 00:14:57,340
I know I shouldn't have come here,

179
00:14:57,350 --> 00:15:01,060
but my father can't sleep in a strange place.

180
00:15:02,120 --> 00:15:03,460
Dad!

181
00:15:03,470 --> 00:15:05,510
Shoes!

182
00:15:06,540 --> 00:15:10,620
You should have prepared for that.

183
00:15:10,620 --> 00:15:14,700
I told you to pull yourself together.

184
00:15:14,710 --> 00:15:18,880
We only have two rooms.

185
00:15:19,400 --> 00:15:22,200
Do Hoon's going to be late.

186
00:15:23,560 --> 00:15:26,000
Take your father to Do Hoon's room.

187
00:15:26,010 --> 00:15:28,210
Thank you, father.

188
00:15:29,220 --> 00:15:31,260
Stop calling him father.

189
00:15:32,760 --> 00:15:35,540
Thank you.

190
00:15:44,030 --> 00:15:53,130
Dad, it's okay. I'll take care of these complicated problems.

191
00:16:10,230 --> 00:16:12,020
Are you going home?

192
00:16:12,030 --> 00:16:13,110
Yes, I am.

193
00:16:13,110 --> 00:16:16,150
I warned you.

194
00:16:16,150 --> 00:16:16,960
Excuse me?

195
00:16:16,970 --> 00:16:20,260
This is nothing personal. Don't complain about me.

196
00:16:20,270 --> 00:16:24,040
This is an organization, and I'm part of this organization.

197
00:16:25,990 --> 00:16:28,390
I'll see you at the Supreme Prosecutor's Office.

198
00:16:36,340 --> 00:16:39,720
I agreed to go on a date with the manager to get you this job.

199
00:16:39,730 --> 00:16:41,670
Don't mess it up.

200
00:16:42,180 --> 00:16:44,850
Thank you, Hae Ri.

201
00:17:18,010 --> 00:17:19,450
Kwang Soo.

202
00:17:19,460 --> 00:17:22,410
- My shoe's untied. - Yes, sir!

203
00:17:55,240 --> 00:18:00,310
Our boss is really young, right?

204
00:18:03,880 --> 00:18:06,170
What's wrong?

205
00:18:06,870 --> 00:18:09,440
What?

206
00:18:10,030 --> 00:18:13,260
I'm really busy at the moment. Hey! Come quick!

207
00:18:14,730 --> 00:18:19,290
You can work here.

208
00:18:32,720 --> 00:18:34,660
Why did you do that?

209
00:18:41,800 --> 00:18:44,870
Stop! That's enough!

210
00:19:13,840 --> 00:19:21,490
Sorry, I don't think I can work here.

211
00:19:21,500 --> 00:19:25,130
Sorry, Hae Ri. I owe you.

212
00:20:02,170 --> 00:20:08,850
I told her that I don't want to see her, how dare she come to my place?

213
00:20:11,930 --> 00:20:13,560
Hello.

214
00:20:15,810 --> 00:20:17,490
Again?

215
00:20:17,630 --> 00:20:19,760
No. I'm coming now.

216
00:20:19,790 --> 00:20:21,720
Sorry.

217
00:20:26,260 --> 00:20:27,860
She is coming up.

218
00:20:27,900 --> 00:20:29,920
She's coming.

219
00:20:46,140 --> 00:20:47,490
Should I follow her?

220
00:20:47,520 --> 00:20:49,030
No.

221
00:20:49,560 --> 00:20:52,430
I had an early meeting. I'm tired.

222
00:20:53,200 --> 00:20:55,000
Let's go.

223
00:20:59,870 --> 00:21:01,700
Ms.

224
00:21:01,700 --> 00:21:02,720
Sorry.

225
00:21:02,720 --> 00:21:04,150
I'm really sorry.

226
00:21:04,150 --> 00:21:06,830
Sorry.

227
00:21:10,700 --> 00:21:14,670
Dad, what are you doing here?

228
00:21:14,670 --> 00:21:16,670
Yoo Jung, open the door.

229
00:21:16,670 --> 00:21:19,170
It's locked.

230
00:21:19,170 --> 00:21:20,870
This isn't our house anymore.

231
00:21:20,870 --> 00:21:21,480
Let's go.

232
00:21:21,480 --> 00:21:23,580
Open the door.

233
00:21:23,580 --> 00:21:27,780
I'll bring you back here later.

234
00:21:27,780 --> 00:21:31,570
Your mother didn't like dessert at first,

235
00:21:32,540 --> 00:21:38,240
but she came to like the bread that I baked.

236
00:21:38,240 --> 00:21:42,190
She liked my creams buns.

237
00:21:42,990 --> 00:21:48,900
Dad! Dad! Dad! Dad!

238
00:21:50,590 --> 00:21:52,470
His blood vessels are swollen.

239
00:21:52,470 --> 00:21:57,480
We need to do a cerebral artery surgery as soon as possible.

240
00:21:57,480 --> 00:22:00,500
I temporarily treated him with medication.

241
00:22:00,500 --> 00:22:04,840
It's like a time bomb.

242
00:22:04,840 --> 00:22:07,950
Will surgery cure him?

243
00:22:07,950 --> 00:22:11,560
That depends on the recovery condition after the surgery.

244
00:22:11,560 --> 00:22:13,990
Do the surgery, please.

245
00:22:14,940 --> 00:22:20,860
Please save my father.

246
00:22:21,510 --> 00:22:24,490
I won't take it off.

247
00:22:24,490 --> 00:22:27,210
Dad, if you fight like this, you might faint again.

248
00:22:27,210 --> 00:22:30,050
Dad, take it off, please!

249
00:22:30,050 --> 00:22:32,200
No!

250
00:22:37,230 --> 00:22:40,420
Dad. Come on!

251
00:22:41,060 --> 00:22:44,350
If you don't put these on, I'll send you back to the nursing home.

252
00:22:44,350 --> 00:22:45,710
Quickly.

253
00:22:45,710 --> 00:22:48,170
Come on! Hand!

254
00:24:08,670 --> 00:24:10,320
Wow!

255
00:24:10,320 --> 00:24:11,630
Take this as collateral.

256
00:24:11,630 --> 00:24:15,340
Take care of it, I'll come back for it.

257
00:24:28,890 --> 00:24:31,010
I'm Park Hyun Suk, a special prosecutor.

258
00:24:31,010 --> 00:24:35,740
Congressman Kim Chang Suk claimed that he's the victim of a sting operation.

259
00:24:35,740 --> 00:24:43,040
We're going to investigate the truth regarding his claim.

260
00:24:43,040 --> 00:24:46,410
Did you submit your statement to the police?

261
00:24:46,410 --> 00:24:48,220
Yes.

262
00:24:55,530 --> 00:24:58,040
Prosecutor Ahn Do Hoon.

263
00:25:00,040 --> 00:25:02,890
Have you got a minute?

264
00:25:22,490 --> 00:25:25,760
This will be your desk.

265
00:25:29,280 --> 00:25:32,980
These are documents related to Congressman Kim's foreign account.

266
00:25:33,830 --> 00:25:37,500
Why are you giving these to me?

267
00:25:37,500 --> 00:25:40,200
Join the K Corporation Legal Team.

268
00:25:40,200 --> 00:25:44,830
Take it as a signing bonus.

269
00:25:44,830 --> 00:25:47,580
Do I look that simply to you?

270
00:25:48,860 --> 00:25:51,560
I don't think so.

271
00:25:51,560 --> 00:25:54,460
I just feel it's urgent

272
00:25:55,530 --> 00:25:59,110
to cuff Congressman Kim one more time.

273
00:25:59,110 --> 00:26:02,290
Submit your letter of resignation.

274
00:26:08,710 --> 00:26:12,230
Dad!

275
00:26:12,230 --> 00:26:13,330
Doctor.

276
00:26:13,330 --> 00:26:14,240
Mr. Kang Woo Chul!

277
00:26:14,240 --> 00:26:16,550
The third one.

278
00:26:16,550 --> 00:26:17,790
Open your eyes.

279
00:26:17,790 --> 00:26:18,540
Grab his arms.

280
00:26:18,540 --> 00:26:19,490
Please wait outside.

281
00:26:19,490 --> 00:26:21,260
Mr. Kang, open your eyes.

282
00:26:21,260 --> 00:26:24,330
- Wait outside. - Grab his arms.

283
00:26:32,470 --> 00:26:34,740
When can I finish it?

284
00:26:34,740 --> 00:26:36,780
I have to stay up today.

285
00:26:36,780 --> 00:26:38,340
Sir.

286
00:26:38,340 --> 00:26:41,380
If you give me the phone and bank records...

287
00:26:41,380 --> 00:26:44,280
I'm not allowed to give you any work

288
00:26:44,280 --> 00:26:47,470
while you're under investigation.

289
00:27:23,490 --> 00:27:26,960
I guess things aren't going so well.

290
00:27:28,980 --> 00:27:32,360
What are you doing here?

291
00:27:37,250 --> 00:27:39,600
Thank you for your handkerchief.

292
00:27:42,280 --> 00:27:44,480
I don't think you're here just to give this back to me.

293
00:27:44,480 --> 00:27:50,530
It sounds like an excuse.

294
00:27:54,330 --> 00:27:57,470
I don't know why I'm here.

295
00:27:57,470 --> 00:28:01,940
I wanted to talk to someone over a drink,

296
00:28:01,940 --> 00:28:05,410
and you popped into my mind.

297
00:28:05,410 --> 00:28:07,860
I'm busy.

298
00:28:07,860 --> 00:28:10,800
I have lots of cases to take care of...

299
00:28:10,800 --> 00:28:12,680
- I... - Mr. Ahn,

300
00:28:12,680 --> 00:28:17,060
You can go home if you have nothing else to do.

301
00:28:24,380 --> 00:28:27,100
How much can you give me?

302
00:28:27,100 --> 00:28:30,440
How much did you pay?

303
00:28:30,440 --> 00:28:32,730
It was a present.

304
00:28:32,730 --> 00:28:37,420
It's delicate and looks good.

305
00:28:37,420 --> 00:28:39,650
Give me as much as you can.

306
00:28:39,650 --> 00:28:43,310
I'll come back for it.

307
00:28:49,300 --> 00:28:51,190
I'd like to reserve a surgery.

308
00:28:51,190 --> 00:28:53,990
I'll pay the rest later.

309
00:29:01,410 --> 00:29:03,660
Ms. Kang Yoo Jung!

310
00:29:04,550 --> 00:29:06,780
Yes?

311
00:29:07,810 --> 00:29:09,870
Who are you?

312
00:29:10,500 --> 00:29:12,200
Who are you?

313
00:29:12,200 --> 00:29:15,860
What are you doing?

314
00:29:19,440 --> 00:29:22,490
Why do you have the ring

315
00:29:22,490 --> 00:29:26,570
that I bought for my future daughter-in-law?

316
00:29:27,360 --> 00:29:31,800
Do you know how much it's worth?

317
00:29:32,240 --> 00:29:37,430
It's a 150 million KRW ring, and you got 4 million KRW?

318
00:29:37,430 --> 00:29:40,540
Why didn't you just keep it?

319
00:29:40,540 --> 00:29:44,100
It has a serial number, and you can't sell it.

320
00:29:44,100 --> 00:29:47,450
Don't you know that you should give the precious thing back to the owner?

321
00:29:47,450 --> 00:29:50,200
Sorry.

322
00:29:50,200 --> 00:29:55,160
I thought my son gave it to a woman he likes, so I brought you here.

323
00:29:55,160 --> 00:29:58,350
But I don't think that's the case.

324
00:29:58,350 --> 00:30:01,500
Report her to the police.

325
00:30:01,500 --> 00:30:05,220
I gave the ring to her.

326
00:30:09,090 --> 00:30:11,320
Let's go!

327
00:30:12,180 --> 00:30:14,620
Get up!

328
00:30:18,390 --> 00:30:20,700
Get up!

329
00:30:26,210 --> 00:30:30,570
I told you not to show up again.

330
00:30:30,570 --> 00:30:34,640
How dare you sell my property?

331
00:30:34,640 --> 00:30:38,550
I'll pay you back.

332
00:30:38,550 --> 00:30:40,730
Everyone can say that.

333
00:30:40,730 --> 00:30:45,180
My father's sick and I needed money for his surgery.

334
00:30:45,180 --> 00:30:47,830
I shouldn't have done it.

335
00:30:47,830 --> 00:30:51,250
I guess I lost my mind.

336
00:30:51,250 --> 00:30:53,900
It's your father this time?

337
00:30:54,420 --> 00:30:56,960
You have no shortage of excuses.

338
00:30:56,960 --> 00:31:00,390
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

339
00:31:00,390 --> 00:31:03,020
Stop saying sorry.

340
00:31:03,020 --> 00:31:04,870
I don't want your apology.

341
00:31:04,870 --> 00:31:07,950
You should suffer as much as I did.

342
00:31:07,950 --> 00:31:13,120
Feel helpless while you lose your loved ones.

343
00:31:13,120 --> 00:31:18,210
You have to realize how painful it is.

344
00:31:18,210 --> 00:31:19,470
Get out!

345
00:31:19,470 --> 00:31:21,550
I'll see you at the police station.

346
00:31:21,550 --> 00:31:24,180
Get out!

347
00:31:48,570 --> 00:31:49,700
I'm wrong.

348
00:31:49,700 --> 00:31:56,370
Hey, let me go.

349
00:31:56,370 --> 00:31:58,370
Please forgive me this once.

350
00:31:58,370 --> 00:32:01,880
I can't let my father go just like that.

351
00:32:01,880 --> 00:32:03,600
You can take me to the police station.

352
00:32:03,600 --> 00:32:06,570
I'll go to prison. I'll pay for what I did.

353
00:32:06,570 --> 00:32:08,660
Can you wait until I see my father get better

354
00:32:08,660 --> 00:32:09,980
after his surgery?

355
00:32:09,980 --> 00:32:12,700
Please.

356
00:32:12,700 --> 00:32:18,100
If you can let me stay with my father...

357
00:32:18,100 --> 00:32:21,550
Get off of me.

358
00:32:21,550 --> 00:32:23,930
Aren't you ashamed?

359
00:32:23,930 --> 00:32:30,720
Np, I can do worse things than this.

360
00:32:31,730 --> 00:32:39,480
I'm ashamed of what I did to that woman.

361
00:32:41,080 --> 00:32:44,090
I don't think I paid for what I did.

362
00:32:44,090 --> 00:32:48,090
I won't forget it as long as I live.

363
00:32:48,090 --> 00:32:50,970
How can I forget?

364
00:32:50,970 --> 00:32:53,880
Don't mention her.

365
00:32:55,630 --> 00:32:59,150
How dare you mention her?

366
00:33:01,760 --> 00:33:09,490
Sorry. I'm so sorry.

367
00:33:09,980 --> 00:33:14,220
Okay, what are you going to do?

368
00:33:14,220 --> 00:33:17,630
If I save your father,

369
00:33:17,630 --> 00:33:21,270
what can you do for me in return?

370
00:33:23,360 --> 00:33:27,230
As you see, I have lots of money.

371
00:33:27,230 --> 00:33:31,510
I can give you money for your father's surgery.

372
00:33:40,380 --> 00:33:42,510
Se Yeon.

373
00:33:45,640 --> 00:33:46,800
What are you doing here?

374
00:33:46,800 --> 00:33:49,310
Nothing.

375
00:33:49,310 --> 00:33:53,510
I just want to speak ill of someone while drinking.

376
00:33:54,600 --> 00:33:57,090
Who is she?

377
00:33:58,490 --> 00:34:01,370
A woman to see me.

378
00:34:03,280 --> 00:34:07,300
This is my friend, Shin Se Yeon.

379
00:34:10,400 --> 00:34:15,750
And that's Prosecutor Ahn Do Hoon.

380
00:34:31,270 --> 00:34:34,830
How about drinking together?

381
00:34:34,830 --> 00:34:37,370
We'd like to have a drink as well.

382
00:34:37,370 --> 00:34:38,700
Sure. Why not?

383
00:34:38,700 --> 00:34:42,690
Where do you want to go? We have a distinguished guest here.

384
00:34:42,690 --> 00:34:48,500
By the way, I'll wire you the money tomorrow.

385
00:34:51,970 --> 00:34:56,800
Thank you.

386
00:34:56,800 --> 00:34:59,240
If you'll excuse me...

387
00:34:59,240 --> 00:35:01,440
Don't go.

388
00:35:06,560 --> 00:35:08,990
I said don't go.

389
00:35:08,990 --> 00:35:12,580
I did you a favor.

390
00:35:12,960 --> 00:35:15,870
Se Yeon, can I take a rain check?

391
00:35:15,870 --> 00:35:18,940
Are you running away?

392
00:35:20,430 --> 00:35:24,090
You don't like drinking?

393
00:35:24,090 --> 00:35:29,660
You shouldn't run away like that.

394
00:35:52,390 --> 00:35:56,770
I guess it's a little awkward to drink with a stranger.

395
00:35:56,770 --> 00:36:03,090
Have we met before?

396
00:36:03,090 --> 00:36:03,920
I don't think so.

397
00:36:03,920 --> 00:36:06,280
Prosecutor Ahn, I'm a little disappointed.

398
00:36:06,280 --> 00:36:11,400
You always reject my invitations to have a drink.

399
00:36:11,820 --> 00:36:14,900
What do you do?

400
00:36:15,730 --> 00:36:21,590
How do you know Min Hyuk?

401
00:36:21,590 --> 00:36:24,060
A personal friend of mine.

402
00:36:24,060 --> 00:36:28,950
She does everything I ask her to do.

403
00:36:30,560 --> 00:36:36,040
Do Hoon, are you nervous sitting next to a lady?

404
00:36:36,040 --> 00:36:37,310
Why aren't you saying anything?

405
00:36:37,310 --> 00:36:40,710
This is unexpected, and I feel awkward.

406
00:36:40,710 --> 00:36:44,160
I gusee we should introduce some girls to you.

407
00:36:44,160 --> 00:36:48,640
He hasn't been on a date for too long.

408
00:36:48,640 --> 00:36:50,220
What do you think of him?

409
00:36:50,220 --> 00:36:51,560
He's still single. Don't you think he's handsome?

410
00:36:51,560 --> 00:36:52,290
Jo Min Hyuk!

411
00:36:52,290 --> 00:36:59,520
I have a boyfriend.

412
00:37:00,590 --> 00:37:07,570
Really? What does he do?

413
00:37:07,570 --> 00:37:17,730
Something great.

414
00:37:19,720 --> 00:37:21,890
Something great?

415
00:37:21,890 --> 00:37:24,970
Excuse me.

416
00:37:38,210 --> 00:37:42,030
Have you known Min Hyuk for a long time?

417
00:37:44,800 --> 00:37:51,630
Do you know that I'm Min Hyuk's fiance?

418
00:37:51,790 --> 00:37:55,110
No. Please don't misunderstand us.

419
00:37:55,110 --> 00:38:02,540
He... He lent me money for my father's surgery.

420
00:38:02,540 --> 00:38:05,290
That's all.

421
00:38:05,520 --> 00:38:09,150
I shouldn't have come here.

422
00:38:09,660 --> 00:38:14,490
I'm glad you knew that.

423
00:38:14,490 --> 00:38:17,800
I'll go now.

424
00:38:27,080 --> 00:38:29,420
What do you think you're doing?

425
00:38:29,420 --> 00:38:31,690
I didn't do anything.

426
00:38:31,690 --> 00:38:35,290
She came to me and asked me for money for her father's surgery.

427
00:38:35,290 --> 00:38:36,730
What can I do?

428
00:38:36,730 --> 00:38:40,660
Although I hate her, her father is innocent.

429
00:38:40,660 --> 00:38:46,310
I don't just let people die like other people.

430
00:38:46,310 --> 00:38:49,380
Don't you think Kang Yoo Jung is so shameless?

431
00:38:49,380 --> 00:38:52,030
She recognized you, didn't she?

432
00:38:52,030 --> 00:38:54,820
She's sitting next to the person

433
00:38:54,820 --> 00:38:58,410
who put her in jail, yet she didn't flinch.

434
00:39:11,020 --> 00:39:14,800
She paid for what she did.

435
00:39:14,800 --> 00:39:16,400
Don't you think you're being too cruel to her?

436
00:39:16,400 --> 00:39:21,220
I don't know why you're defending her like this.

437
00:39:21,220 --> 00:39:25,880
She's not a criminal anymore.

438
00:39:25,880 --> 00:39:29,370
She's just a citizen who paid for what she did.

439
00:39:29,370 --> 00:39:33,820
What are you talking about?

440
00:39:35,510 --> 00:39:39,460
I don't feel comfortable staying here.

441
00:39:39,460 --> 00:39:44,870
You think you can manipulate people with money.

442
00:39:44,870 --> 00:39:49,680
It makes me sick.

443
00:39:58,270 --> 00:40:04,540
Is she the one who killed Seo Ji Hee?

444
00:40:04,940 --> 00:40:08,190
I'm sorry, it's just...

445
00:40:08,190 --> 00:40:14,260
Min Hyuk! You're not doing this for her.

446
00:40:14,260 --> 00:40:17,920
You just want to arouse others' sympathy so you can do everything you want.

447
00:40:17,920 --> 00:40:25,100
I won't marry you if you keep doing this.

448
00:40:25,100 --> 00:40:28,780
If you think our marriage is business,

449
00:40:30,380 --> 00:40:34,830
try to have a little bit of respect for me.

450
00:40:58,650 --> 00:41:02,080
Excuse me. Have you seen my father?

451
00:41:02,080 --> 00:41:05,040
No.

452
00:41:32,670 --> 00:41:34,980
What do you think you're doing?

453
00:41:34,980 --> 00:41:36,930
How can you beg him for money?

454
00:41:36,930 --> 00:41:37,940
Do you know who he is?

455
00:41:37,940 --> 00:41:42,300
Do Hoon! My father is missing.

456
00:41:42,300 --> 00:41:44,890
He's neither at the hospital nor the bakery.

457
00:41:44,890 --> 00:41:47,560
I didn't find him at the bakery, that's where he goes everytime.

458
00:41:47,560 --> 00:41:48,600
What are you talking about?

459
00:41:48,600 --> 00:41:50,940
My father has disappeared.

460
00:41:50,940 --> 00:41:52,650
Maybe he went to mom's grave.

461
00:41:52,650 --> 00:41:53,680
He sometimes goes there.

462
00:41:53,680 --> 00:41:54,850
I should go there.

463
00:41:54,850 --> 00:41:55,520
Let me go!

464
00:41:55,520 --> 00:41:56,330
Yoo Jung!

465
00:41:56,330 --> 00:41:57,420
My father is missing.

466
00:41:57,420 --> 00:41:59,140
I'll look for him. Calm down.

467
00:41:59,140 --> 00:42:01,480
How can I calm down when my father's missing?

468
00:42:01,480 --> 00:42:04,560
He needs to have surgery. I need to find him.

469
00:42:04,560 --> 00:42:07,450
Report him missing at the police station first.

470
00:42:07,450 --> 00:42:10,860
I'll look for him.

471
00:42:44,640 --> 00:42:45,880
Sir,

472
00:42:47,320 --> 00:42:49,530
please find my father.

473
00:42:50,280 --> 00:42:52,160
He has to do the surgery right away.

474
00:42:52,160 --> 00:42:53,180
I have to find him quickly.

475
00:42:53,180 --> 00:42:55,630
Calm down.

476
00:42:55,630 --> 00:42:58,360
Fill out this form first.

477
00:43:15,140 --> 00:43:16,140
Father.

478
00:43:17,270 --> 00:43:19,920
I don't know where my house is.

479
00:43:19,920 --> 00:43:21,410
Take me to Yoo Jung.

480
00:43:21,410 --> 00:43:23,100
Yes, Yoo Jung's worried about you.

481
00:43:23,100 --> 00:43:24,410
Get in the car.

482
00:43:38,250 --> 00:43:39,610
Thank god!

483
00:43:39,610 --> 00:43:41,840
Drive carefully.

484
00:43:42,250 --> 00:43:43,620
Yes, father.

485
00:43:43,620 --> 00:43:45,900
I mean it.

486
00:43:46,620 --> 00:43:49,880
You hurt Yoo Jung's forehead before.

487
00:43:51,640 --> 00:43:57,430
It rained so heavily that day,

488
00:43:57,430 --> 00:44:01,940
I was worried.

489
00:44:01,940 --> 00:44:04,750
The car was badly damaged.

490
00:44:04,750 --> 00:44:08,920
Thankfully Yoo Jung seemed okay.

491
00:44:10,630 --> 00:44:14,110
You still remember that?

492
00:44:15,640 --> 00:44:18,370
Why not?

493
00:44:18,370 --> 00:44:20,640
You drove that night,

494
00:44:20,640 --> 00:44:23,920
You think I don't know that Yoo Jung is your scrapegoat?

495
00:44:36,780 --> 00:44:39,530
If you do that again,

496
00:44:39,530 --> 00:44:42,370
I won't forgive you.

497
00:44:42,370 --> 00:44:44,650
Do you understand?

498
00:44:45,070 --> 00:44:46,930
Drive safely.

499
00:45:00,350 --> 00:45:05,260
Drive carefully.

500
00:45:37,540 --> 00:45:39,480
Let's call it a day.

501
00:45:39,480 --> 00:45:40,200
Thank you.

502
00:45:40,200 --> 00:45:43,580
-Thank you. -Thank you.

503
00:45:47,380 --> 00:45:49,320
See you tomorrow at 10 a.m.

504
00:45:49,320 --> 00:45:51,600
Prosecutor Ahn Do Hoon.

505
00:45:54,550 --> 00:45:57,980
Are these the principles you talked about?

506
00:45:58,510 --> 00:46:00,780
You said I needed to be flexible

507
00:46:00,780 --> 00:46:02,780
to maintain the principles in this organization.

508
00:46:02,780 --> 00:46:06,680
I didn't know you meant that you would destroy your colleague to get ahead.

509
00:46:06,680 --> 00:46:09,950
Why didn't you tell me that I should forget about principles and truth,

510
00:46:09,950 --> 00:46:11,570
and concentrate on being successful?

511
00:46:11,570 --> 00:46:13,680
You should just tell me that.

512
00:46:13,680 --> 00:46:17,950
Do you think you're clean and just?

513
00:46:17,950 --> 00:46:19,670
That's not true.

514
00:46:20,460 --> 00:46:22,750
I heard how you obtained those files

515
00:46:22,750 --> 00:46:24,950
on Congressman Kim.

516
00:46:26,390 --> 00:46:28,380
Did you go after him

517
00:46:28,380 --> 00:46:30,790
only to reveal the truth?

518
00:46:30,790 --> 00:46:32,800
I don't think so.

519
00:46:32,800 --> 00:46:34,330
You wanted to develop your career

520
00:46:34,330 --> 00:46:37,440
by catching a big fish.

521
00:46:37,440 --> 00:46:39,730
Can you deny that?

522
00:47:09,120 --> 00:47:13,160
Hello.

523
00:47:13,930 --> 00:47:16,830
Yes. Red jacket.

524
00:47:21,280 --> 00:47:23,240
Yes.

525
00:47:23,240 --> 00:47:25,150
Where did you find him?

526
00:47:26,050 --> 00:47:30,170
What? Pohang?

527
00:47:38,370 --> 00:47:40,390
Well...

528
00:47:40,390 --> 00:47:43,390
Thank you for letting the ring incident slide.

529
00:47:43,390 --> 00:47:45,470
Thank you very much.

530
00:47:46,270 --> 00:47:50,060
I'll pay you back even if it takes me my entire life.

531
00:47:50,060 --> 00:47:52,050
I'm in a hurry at the moment.

532
00:47:52,050 --> 00:47:53,440
Sorry.

533
00:47:57,020 --> 00:47:59,760
Please give me a break.

534
00:47:59,760 --> 00:48:01,410
They found my father.

535
00:48:01,410 --> 00:48:02,600
Where is he?

536
00:48:02,990 --> 00:48:04,390
Pohang.

537
00:48:10,530 --> 00:48:12,440
Darn it.

538
00:48:12,440 --> 00:48:13,520
Taxi!

539
00:48:16,670 --> 00:48:18,350
You said Pohang.

540
00:49:38,370 --> 00:49:44,370
Dad. Dad. Dad.

541
00:49:46,650 --> 00:49:48,200
Why?

542
00:49:48,200 --> 00:49:49,570
Oh my god! Dad!

543
00:49:49,570 --> 00:49:55,150
Dad! Dad! Dad!

544
00:50:05,480 --> 00:50:12,320
Dad! Dad! Dad!

545
00:50:12,560 --> 00:50:14,330
Please say something.

546
00:50:14,330 --> 00:50:16,460
This is a typical sting operation

547
00:50:16,460 --> 00:50:19,130
by the prosecution.

548
00:50:19,130 --> 00:50:21,550
They were trying to end my career as a politician.

549
00:50:21,550 --> 00:50:25,160
We have found out the truth.

550
00:50:25,160 --> 00:50:32,460
We're going to...

551
00:50:48,340 --> 00:50:50,650
You came straight here.

552
00:50:50,650 --> 00:50:53,880
No one's waiting for me anyway.

553
00:50:54,170 --> 00:50:55,000
I'll go get some tofu.

554
00:50:55,000 --> 00:50:56,130
Stop!

555
00:50:56,130 --> 00:50:58,080
Do you want to advertise that I got out of jail?

556
00:50:58,080 --> 00:50:59,230
That's ridiculous.

557
00:50:59,230 --> 00:51:01,450
Do you think tofu will make me clean?

558
00:51:13,010 --> 00:51:14,810
It's not that bad.

559
00:51:14,810 --> 00:51:17,350
There's someone else crying instead of you.

560
00:51:17,860 --> 00:51:19,370
Have you found an accomodation yet?

561
00:51:19,370 --> 00:51:20,600
Unbelievable!

562
00:51:20,600 --> 00:51:22,470
Are you worried about me?

563
00:51:22,470 --> 00:51:24,260
I can find a place to stay.

564
00:51:24,260 --> 00:51:27,190
If you have nowhere else to go, go find me.

565
00:51:36,930 --> 00:51:37,980
What?

566
00:51:37,980 --> 00:51:40,030
Are you waiting for someone?

567
00:51:45,470 --> 00:51:47,490
I don't like it.

568
00:51:47,490 --> 00:51:51,080
You always smile like that when you're tired.

569
00:52:45,610 --> 00:52:50,040
Take it. It's all I have.

570
00:52:54,910 --> 00:53:00,560
I'll feel a little bit better this way.

571
00:53:02,870 --> 00:53:08,680
I thought a lot in the mourning hall.

572
00:53:09,700 --> 00:53:12,440
When is he coming?

573
00:53:12,440 --> 00:53:17,160
Will he come today? Will he come in the midnight?

574
00:53:18,960 --> 00:53:22,650
I waited and waited, but you never came.

575
00:53:25,130 --> 00:53:31,980
I was thinking, if you came on the 1st day,

576
00:53:31,990 --> 00:53:36,430
I would've relied on you too much,

577
00:53:36,960 --> 00:53:42,390
and I wouldn't have said a proper good-bye to dad.

578
00:53:44,640 --> 00:53:45,920
Yoo Jung.

579
00:53:45,940 --> 00:53:53,880
If you came on the 2nd day, I would've blame you for not coming earlier.

580
00:53:53,880 --> 00:53:57,830
I wouldn't have thought about dad.

581
00:54:01,830 --> 00:54:07,240
Thank you for coming today.

582
00:54:09,190 --> 00:54:13,090
I'm glad that I saw you.

583
00:54:14,340 --> 00:54:15,990
Sorry.

584
00:54:16,010 --> 00:54:24,840
Let's break up.

585
00:54:30,680 --> 00:54:37,350
It's been so hard for both of us, right?

586
00:54:37,390 --> 00:54:38,220
Yoo Jung.

587
00:54:38,230 --> 00:54:46,850
We've tried not to hurt each other, and we just smile.

588
00:54:46,860 --> 00:54:52,120
This isn't right.

589
00:54:52,130 --> 00:54:55,720
Every time you see me, you'll feel guilty,

590
00:54:55,730 --> 00:54:59,380
and you'll try to do something for me.

591
00:54:59,400 --> 00:55:03,770
I'll be uncomfortable looking at you.

592
00:55:04,190 --> 00:55:08,120
It'll repeat.

593
00:55:09,570 --> 00:55:17,220
But I don't regret what I did.

594
00:55:18,510 --> 00:55:25,460
Even if I could do it all over again, I'd do the same thing.

595
00:55:25,850 --> 00:55:29,490
Stop feeling guilty because of that.

596
00:55:32,280 --> 00:55:39,800
What can I do for you?

597
00:55:54,100 --> 00:55:57,460
Let me leave first.

598
00:55:59,720 --> 00:56:07,270
If I leave first, you would remember me for a long time.

599
00:56:07,840 --> 00:56:13,900
I don't think I can watch you walk away.

600
00:56:14,790 --> 00:56:18,610
I can't bear to watch.

601
00:57:34,360 --> 00:57:42,330
I should've bought you good shoes.

602
00:58:12,810 --> 00:58:16,730
I shouldn't take busy as an excuse.

603
00:58:17,470 --> 00:58:24,930
I wish I had gone to see the autumn leaves when you asked me to.

604
00:58:26,510 --> 00:58:30,790
I wish I had spent more time talking to you.

605
00:58:30,800 --> 00:58:35,990
I wish I had said these things more often.

606
00:58:51,180 --> 00:58:58,000
Dad, you made delicious bread.

607
00:59:00,810 --> 00:59:05,600
It was the most delicious bread in the world.

608
00:59:23,700 --> 00:59:31,070
I shouldn't have washed it. I can't smell him anymore.

609
00:59:40,080 --> 00:59:45,430
Dad. Dad.

610
00:59:46,200 --> 00:59:49,640
Dad.

611
01:00:01,130 --> 01:00:09,890
Dad, next time, be born as my child.

612
01:00:09,920 --> 01:00:13,440
I'll take care of you.

613
01:00:15,370 --> 01:00:19,480
I'll do everything that you did for me.

614
01:00:21,220 --> 01:00:25,580
I'll pay back.

615
01:00:29,830 --> 01:00:38,430
What should I do, dad?

616
01:00:48,770 --> 01:00:54,410
What should I do, dad?

617
01:00:57,580 --> 01:00:59,010
Where is Kang Yoo Jung?

618
01:00:59,010 --> 01:01:01,250
I haven't seen her for days.

619
01:01:01,260 --> 01:01:03,380
Find her.

620
01:01:03,390 --> 01:01:04,090
Yes.

621
01:01:04,100 --> 01:01:06,210
No. Forget it.

622
01:01:06,220 --> 01:01:09,320
You're no good at finding people.

623
01:02:19,750 --> 01:02:23,840
Hey! Hey!

624
01:02:24,850 --> 01:02:25,950
Hey! Wake up!

625
01:02:25,960 --> 01:02:30,010
Wake up!

626
01:02:47,920 --> 01:02:53,960
Wake up!

627
01:03:11,740 --> 01:03:15,050
Here! Over here!

628
01:03:15,060 --> 01:03:16,100
- She's dying. - Come this way.

629
01:03:16,110 --> 01:03:18,130
This way.

630
01:04:09,330 --> 01:04:12,550
Don't die.

631
01:04:12,560 --> 01:04:17,520
Don't die without my permission.
